Letting $x=2$, we get the series:

$\begin{align}
\displaystyle\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty } \dfrac{(2-3)^n}{n^2}
 &=\displaystyle\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty }\dfrac{(-1)^n}{n^2}
\end{align}$

By the alternating series test, we know this series converges.

Letting $x=4$, we get the series:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{(4-3)^n}{n^2}
 &=\displaystyle\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty }\dfrac{1}{n^2}
\end{align}$

By the $p$-series test, we know this series converges.
